  "notes": "This is a cloud-rental price comparison (US$ per GPU-hour, on-demand), not a hardware purchase-price series, so it contextualizes rather than directly confirms Newegg's one-off $34,879 H100 card listing and out-of-stock H200. Both provider pages (nvidia-h100 and nvidia-h200) are on the same site, getdeploying.com, and each independently states a same-day median: H100 median $3.32/GPU-hr (stated as of 2026-09-06) and H200 median $4.40/GPU-hr (stated as of 2026-09-07). Where a provider listed a range or multiple tiers (e.g. spot vs reserved vs on-demand) rather than one bare on-demand figure, that provider was left out per rule 9; only providers with one clean number per GPU on each page were kept. The pattern -- H200 consistently priced at or above H100 across nearly every matched provider -- is directionally consistent with H200 being the scarcer, harder-to-source part referenced in the bullet, though this series speaks to cloud rental economics, not retail card availability.",
  "bulletIndex": 3
